  ('Proximity', 5, 'noun', '/prɒkˈsɪm.ə.ti/', 'Nearness in space, time, or relationship.', 'Yaqinlik, qo''shnilik', 'Близость, соседство', 'The apartment''s close proximity to the central subway station made it highly attractive to renters.', 'Kvartiraning markaziy metro bekatiga yaqinligi uni ijarachilar uchun juda jozibador qildi.', '["in close proximity to","geographical proximity","proximity of danger"]'::jsonb, '["nearness","closeness","vicinity","adjacency"]'::jsonb, 95),
  ('Publicity', 5, 'noun', '/pʌbˈlɪs.ə.ti/', 'Notice or attention given to someone or something by the media.', 'Ommaviylik, reklama, jamoat e''tibori', 'Публичность, известность, реклама', 'The new film received massive global publicity thanks to viral social media marketing campaigns.', 'Yangi film ijtimoiy tarmoqlardagi virusli marketing kampaniyalari tufayli katta ommaviy e''tibor qozondi.', '["bad publicity","seek publicity","publicity campaign"]'::jsonb, '["attention","exposure","media coverage","hype"]'::jsonb, 96),
  ('Remedy', 5, 'noun', '/ˈrem.ə.di/', 'A medicine or treatment for a disease or injury; also a means of counteracting or solving an undesirable situation.', 'Davo, chora, shifo', 'Лекарство, средство, исправление', 'Hot tea with honey and lemon is a traditional, time-tested home remedy for a sore throat.', 'Asal va limonli issiq choy tomoq og''rig''i uchun an''anaviy va vaqt sinovidan o''tgan uy shifosidir.', '["home remedy","legal remedy","effective remedy"]'::jsonb, '["cure","treatment","solution","antidote"]'::jsonb, 97),
