  ('Proficient', 6, 'adjective', '/prəˈfɪʃ.ənt/', 'Competent or skilled in doing or using something.', 'Mohir, puxta o''zlashtirgan, usta', 'Опытный, искусный, сведущий', 'To secure a managerial position, you must be proficient in both spoken and written English.', 'Boshqaruv lavozimini egallash uchun siz ingliz tilida ham og''zaki, ham yozma ravishda mohir bo''lishingiz kerak.', '["proficient in English","highly proficient","become proficient"]'::jsonb, '["skilled","expert","adept","competent"]'::jsonb, 116),
  ('Quest', 6, 'noun', '/kwest/', 'A long or arduous search for something valuable or meaningful.', 'Izlanish, qidiruv, intilish', 'Поиск, стремление', 'Scientists continue their tireless quest to find an effective, universal cure for cancer.', 'Olimlar saratonga qarshi samarali, umumiy davoni topish bo''yicha charchoqsiz izlanishlarini davom ettirmoqdalar.', '["in quest of","spiritual quest","quest for knowledge"]'::jsonb, '["search","pursuit","hunt","mission"]'::jsonb, 117),
  ('Ridge', 6, 'noun', '/rɪdʒ/', 'A long, narrow hilltop, mountain range, or elevated land strip.', 'Tog'' qirrasi, qirra', 'Хребет, гребень горы', 'The mountaineers walked carefully along the narrow razor-sharp ridge of the mountain.', 'Alpinistlar tog''ning tor va o''tkir qirrasi bo''ylab ehtiyotkorlik bilan qadam tashladilar.', '["mountain ridge","along the ridge","rocky ridge"]'::jsonb, '["crest","hilltop","spine","edge"]'::jsonb, 118),
